Mark the plymouth argument as used when systemd support is disabled

dnf5's offline reboot helper only uses the plymouth output object inside a
WITH_SYSTEMD block.  Building with -DWITH_SYSTEMD=OFF therefore trips
-Wunused-parameter (promoted to an error in the project's build flags).

--- a/dnf5/commands/offline/offline.cpp
+++ b/dnf5/commands/offline/offline.cpp
@@ -276,6 +276,7 @@
 }
 
 void reboot(bool poweroff = false, PlymouthOutput * plymouth = nullptr) {
+    (void)plymouth;
     if (std::getenv("DNF_SYSTEM_UPGRADE_NO_REBOOT")) {
         if (poweroff) {
             std::cerr << "DNF_SYSTEM_UPGRADE_NO_REBOOT is set, not powering off." << std::endl;
